<USER_REQUEST>
Calculate the entropy change (J/mol K) of the given reaction. The molar entropies [J/K mol] are given in brackets after each substance.

\[ 2 \text{PbS(s)} [91.2] + 3 \text{O}_2(g) [205.1] \rightarrow 2 \text{PbO(s)} [66.5] + 2 \text{SO}_2(g) [248.2] \]
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
To calculate the entropy change (ΔS) for the given reaction, we can use the following formula:

ΔS = ΣS_products - ΣS_reactants

For the given reaction:

\[ 2 \text{PbS(s)} + 3 \text{O}_2(g) \rightarrow 2 \text{PbO(s)} + 2 \text{SO}_2(g) \]

The molar entropies are:

- PbS(s): 91.2 J/K mol
- O2(g): 205.1 J/K mol
- PbO(s): 66.5 J/K mol
- SO2(g): 248.2 J/K mol

Now, we can calculate the entropy change:

ΔS = (2 * S_PbO + 2 * S_SO2) - (2 * S_PbS + 3 * S_O2)

ΔS = (2 * 66.5 J/K mol + 2 * 248.2 J/K mol) - (2 * 91.2 J/K mol + 3 * 205.1 J/K mol)

ΔS = (133.0 J/K mol + 496.4 J/K mol) - (182.4 J/K mol + 615.3 J/K mol)

ΔS = 629.4 J/K mol - 797.7 J/K mol

ΔS = -168.3 J/K mol

The entropy change for the reaction is -168.3 J/K mol.
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

