A solution has a hydronium ion concentration \([H_3O^+]\) of \(10^{-4}\) M. What is the nature of this solution (acidic, basic, or neutral)?
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The pH of a solution is calculated as:  
\[
\text{pH} = -\log[H_3O^+]
\]  
Given \([H_3O^+] = 10^{-4}\) M, the pH is:  
\[
\text{pH} = -\log(10^{-4}) = -(-4) = 4
\]  
A solution is acidic if its pH is less than 7, basic if its pH is greater than 7, and neutral if its pH is equal to 7.  
Since the pH is \(\boxed{4}\), the solution is \(\boxed{\text{acidic}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

