- \( f \) is the force of friction
- \( \mu \) is the coefficient of friction
- \( N \) is the normal force.

The dimensions of force are \([MLT^{-2}]\) and the dimensions of normal force are also \([MLT^{-2}\] because it is a force. Substituting these dimensions:

\[ [M L T^{-2}] = [\mu] [M L T^{-2}] \]

