We have 2.5 moles of propane. To find the total heat released, we can multiply the number of moles of propane by the standard enthalpy of combustion:

Heat released = (moles of propane) × (standard enthalpy of combustion)
Heat released = 2.5 moles × -2220 kJ/mol
Heat released = -5550 kJ

