\]

where:
- \( I_{\text{reflected}} \) is the intensity of the reflected light.
- \( I_{\text{induced}} \) is the intensity of the emitted light.
- \( I_{\text{absorbed}} \) is the intensity of the absorbed light.
- \( I_{\text{incident}} \) is the incident incident light intensity.
- \( I_s \) is the saturation intensity, given by \( I_s = \frac{\hbar \omega}{3\pi \epsilon_0 A} \), where \( \hbar \) is the reduced Planck constant, \( \omega \) is the frequency of the light, and \( \epsilon_0 \) is the permittivity of free space.
- \( R_0 \) is the intensity ratio of spontaneous emission to absorption at thermal equilibrium, given by \( R_0 = \frac{B I_{\text{absorbed}}}{J_0} \), where \( J_0 \) is the intensity of the incident radiation at thermal equilibrium.

