2. **Spontaneous Emission:** The excited atoms can spontaneously emit light, emitting photons in all directions. The rate of spontaneous emission is proportional to the coefficient \( A \).

3. **Stimulated Emission:** The incident incident light can also stimulate the excited atoms to emit more light at the same frequency and phase, enhancing the reflected intensity. The rate of stimulated emission is proportional to the intensity \( I \) of the incident light and the coefficient \( B \).

