","(a) The force on the proton is given by \(F = qE\), where \(q\) is the charge and \(E\) is the electric field strength. The force is \(F = (1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C})(500 \, \text{N/C}) = 8.0 \times 10^{-17} \, \text{N}\).  
Using Newton's second law, \(F = ma\), we find the acceleration:
\[
a = \frac{F}{m} = \frac{8.0 \times 10^{-17} \, \text{N}}{1.67 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{kg}} = 4.79 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2.
\]

