\[
\Delta S = \frac{Q}{T}
\]
where \( \Delta S \) is the change in entropy and \( Q \) is the heat generated.

The work done by friction is \( W = F_{\text{fr}} \Delta x \), where \( \Delta x \) is the distance over which friction acts. The work done by friction is converted into heat \( Q = W \). The change in velocity is \( \Delta v = v \Delta t \), so \( \Delta x = v \Delta t \). Thus, \( Q = F_{\text{fr}} v \Delta t \).

